{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Do not eat of it raw.</b> Ibn Ezra explains: since 'the abomination of Egypt you shall sacrifice,' perhaps you will say: let us not roast it fully, lest the Egyptians notice it — therefore it says: 'Do not eat of it raw.' And perhaps you will say: let us boil it and hide it in a pot — therefore it says: 'בשל מבושל' ('boiled'). And perhaps you will say: let us cut off the head and the legs so they will not recognize what it is — therefore it says: 'ראשו על כרעיו ועל קרבו' ('its head upon its legs and upon its innards')."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:58.461701706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}